<li>It might not be celebrated across the U.S., but for those who know about Sweetest Day, it can be a big deal. Apparently a really, really big deal. According to Retail Confectioners International, a trade association made up of chocolate and candy makers, some of its members report that Sweetest Day candy sales are bigger than those for Mothers Day. The cities of Detroit, Cleveland and Buffalo are among the biggest Sweetest Day celebrators.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<h2><strong>Sweetest Day Symbols</strong></h2>
<p>The gifts that were given early on for sweetest day were candy and flowers mostly, but then expanded to be any variety of treats.</p>
<p>The thought behind <strong>Sweetest Day</strong> is to spend the day doing kind things for those you love. That can take the form of a good deed or a favor, but most of the time, it ends up being gifts that are given. And what\'s a popular gift to give to show sweetness? Candy! Valentine\'s Day may have cornered the market on red roses and chocolate, but Sweetest Day is the day to give gummy bears and other sweet goodies.</p>';
